Z||000000||lesgiannini||09-30-1999||06:57 PM||||1st: when I push the horn button the interior lights come on AND the radio switches from FM to AM. Also if I open either door while the radio is on it goes off.<BR>2nd I found,that, when lifting the hood for the first time, in that little space in- between the front fascia a part of the frame is slightly bent. How do you repair that part of the frame? The fascia support is OK,<BR>the hood seems a little to far away from the fascia but it closes. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mwbackus||09-30-1999||07:46 PM||||Check all of your fuses very closely.  I have heard that conditions such as this may be due to transient voltage from a bad fuse or short.  The worst case would be the enormous expense usually incurred to rid your car of a demonic possesion. (just kidding)<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000002||WGraffiKs||09-30-1999||08:00 PM||||I agree with MW.  I had a similar problem with my 86, seemed just like demonic possession, until I exorcized it by replacing the open fuse,which, as I recall, had nothing to do with any of the circuits involved.  Good Luck!||||reg||4
Z||000003||lowCG||09-30-1999||08:08 PM||||I would start at the fuse panel,and make sure everything is good there,then maybe the headlight switch,or something shorted in the underhood lights.<BR>Had a similar problem once when my old Porsche had a couple wires crossed in the trunk;the guages would all peg when the brakes were applied.<BR>Maybe to remove one fuse at a time,to try and find the problem,would be another thing to do,I would get a schematic and follow the flow of power in any circuit that is suspect.||||reg||1
